                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This game has lots of potential, and i purchased it assuming the complaints in the negative reviews had been fixed by this point. notice this review is march 2017. the issues are not fixed. i refunded due to multiple bugs, the worst of which is the game randomly deciding it wont recognize player 2's inputs, regardless of controller or port, working one second, and then not the next. there are other glaring issues as well that i figured the developers would have worked on, and they havent, including no proper menus or tutorial, no mini maps, no proper anything. hell, you will spend your first 30 minutes just trying to figure out how to select game mode, map, how to connect player 2, all the simplest shit that could be done in 2 seconds with a regular menu. they make you drive around a gigantic map, driving through \"option\" portals and \"option\" pickups that are not labeled, or even modeled after what youd expect the option to look like, and senselessly spread around, its insanity. the devs are not interested in listening to the community, the game has potential, but everything else causes it to be a NO BUY from me. try if you like, but you will quickly request a refund. it really is as bad as the other negs say.",
